#: rc.cpp:492
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<p>Preemphasis is mainly used in audio processing. Higher frequencies in audio "
"signals usually have lower amplitudes. This can lead to bad signal quality on "
"noisy transmission because the high frequencies might become too weak. To avoid "
"this effect, high frequencies are amplified before transmission (preemphasis); "
"the receiver will then weaken them accordingly for playback."
msgstr ""
"Vörvertarren warrt tomehrst in de digitale Signaalverarbeiden bruukt.\n"
"Högere Frequenzen vun Audiosignalen hebbt tomehrst sietere Amplituden.\n"
"Dit kann de Signaalgööd bi Överdregen mit veel Rusen leeg maken, wiel de hogen "
"Frequenzen to swack warrn köönt. Dit lett sik ümgahn, wenn de hogen Frequenzen "
"ehr't Överdregen stärker (Vörvertarren) un achteran wedder swacher maakt warrt."

